# Cloudflare Pages rewrite: /app/<username> is a route, not a file on disk.
# Status 200 is a rewrite (the URL stays put) rather than a redirect, which is what
# boot.js reads to determine the route.
#
# IMPORTANT: no executable assets may live under /app/. Pages follows redirects
# "regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming request" -- unlike Netlify,
# an existing file does NOT win over a splat. boot.js and app.js therefore sit at the
# public/ root; if they were under /app/ this rule would serve index.html for them with
# content-type text/html, the module MIME check would reject the script, and every page
# would render blank.
/app      /app/index.html   200
/app/*    /app/index.html   200
